  "id": "COMPOUND:34580 - PROTEIN:6294",
  "verbalization": "Isoswinholide B appears to interact with Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Isoswinholide B directly targets U-87 MG, a cell line that in turn is targeted by (2S)-3',4'-Dihydroxy-6,7-Dimethoxyflavan, which itself targets the enzyme in question. Similarly, Isoswinholide B also targets Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13 and Serine/threonine-protein kinase Nek5, both of which are involved in targeting the same enzyme. These findings indicate that Isoswinholide B may exert its effects through multiple pathways that ultimately converge on the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6. The overlapping targets suggest a potential mechanism of action involving kinase signaling or metabolic regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
